## STEP 0 — Build a verification tree instead of checking out here

**CRITICAL:** This checkout is shared with other review-role agents that may be
running concurrently. Do **NOT** switch branches or flip HEAD in this directory
via `gh pr` or `git` — doing so races with a sibling agent verifying a different
PR at the same time (D#1684). Use the sanctioned mechanism for read-only roles
instead — it clones the PR head into a separate, write-protected tree outside
this checkout:

```bash
source scripts/lib/verify-tree.sh
source scripts/lib/repo-resolve.sh

# Resolve the CODE plane's git remote — never fetch a PR ref from the bare
# name "origin", which is the Discussion plane. PR numbers collide across
# the two planes, and a wrong-plane fetch succeeds silently (D#1940 FM-5).
CODE_REMOTE=$(_resolve_code_plane_remote) || { echo "FAIL: could not resolve the code-plane git remote"; exit 1; }

PR_SHA=$(gh pr view {{pr_number}} --repo {{CODE_REPO}} --json headRefOid --jq .headRefOid)
git fetch --quiet "$CODE_REMOTE" "pull/{{pr_number}}/head"

TREE_BASE="$(mktemp -d)"
DEST="$TREE_BASE/pr-{{pr_number}}"
verify_tree_build "$PR_SHA" "$DEST" || { echo "FAIL: could not build verification tree for PR #{{pr_number}}"; exit 1; }
```

After building, verify the tree landed on the expected commit. A mismatch is
a hard abort, not a warning — a tree on the wrong commit invalidates every
result measured in it:

```bash
# Confirm the tree's HEAD matches the PR's expected headRefOid
HEAD_SHA=$(git -C "$DEST" rev-parse HEAD)
[ "$HEAD_SHA" = "$PR_SHA" ] || { echo "FAIL: tree HEAD mismatch — $HEAD_SHA vs expected $PR_SHA — refusing to test the wrong commit"; exit 1; }
echo "OK: tree is on PR head"
```

Run every subsequent step (test suite, lint, build) *inside* `$DEST`, e.g.
`(cd "$DEST" && {test command})`. After each run, call
`verify_tree_assert "$DEST" "$PR_SHA"` from OUTSIDE the tree — it catches drift
(another writer landed in `$DEST`, or content silently changed underneath the run)
and voids that run's results if it fails.

Never run tests against this checkout's local `main` — it goes stale within
minutes on a busy day, and testing against it yields a false pass or fail
that has nothing to do with the PR under review. `$DEST` built above is the
only tree that is guaranteed NOT stale.

Do **NOT** run any tests until `verify_tree_build` succeeds and the HEAD check above
confirms `OK`.

